+You can also use `yield` directly in your *path operation function* to stream the response. If you declare `response_class=StreamingResponse`, the data will be streamed as is. If you don't declare a `response_class`, FastAPI will stream the data as [JSON Lines](../tutorial/stream-json-lines.md){.internal-link target=_blank}.
+
 /// note | Technical Details
 
 An `async` task can only be cancelled when it reaches an `await`. If there is no `await`, the generator (function with `yield`) can not be cancelled properly and may keep running even after cancellation is requested.
